# The Windows delivery is text that Windows itself has to parse, so its line
# endings are part of the payload, not a formatting preference.
#
# cmd.exe reads a .bat one line at a time and is documented to work with CRLF.
# With LF only it usually copes - and then does not: a goto that lands one byte
# past its label, or a parenthesised if-block that swallows the line after it.
# The failure is silent and happens on someone else's machine.
#
# "-text" means: never convert these, in either direction. They are stored with
# CRLF and they leave the repository with CRLF - including through the
# `git archive` that builds the Windows bundle.
*.bat            -text
*.iss            -text
packaging/*.txt  -text
